>and if we were actually trying to do a real dictionary, we'd need to
>have entries, or sub-entries, for each of those meanings.

My original intent was to do exactly that, using a commonly available 
dictionary as the source of word meanings.  Given their availability, I 
would probably use one of the out-of-copyright dictionaries now available 
on the net, which would have such information for words and definitions 
used prior to 75 years ago.

But space would make this impossible (even if the volunteers were 
available) - the resulting text would necessarily be longer than the 
English-only dictionary, since it would have all that text as well as the 
Lojban.  Printing costs are too high to include an English dictionary in 
with the E-L dictionary.

